{"title":"2018 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_-_Complementary_Counting\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 - Complementary Counting</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Using_Answer_Choices)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Using Answer Choices)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f8440824a9efceca3bac830578ab38c27957f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> contain at least one prime number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/d/05d427bab402137a284ba218a7385a2054e268d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\text{ 128} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)} \\text{ 192} \\qquad \\textbf{(C)} \\text{ 224} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)} \\text{ 240} \\qquad \\textbf{(E)} \\text{ 256}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"428\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_-_Complementary_Counting\">Solution 1 - Complementary Counting</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 - Complementary Counting\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use complementary counting, or \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/7/4c7bd6550e6179156059d67a831b78df0c09de69.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{total - what we don&#39;t want = what we want}$\" width=\"319\" height=\"12\" />. \n</p><p>There are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/1635abf3f228d02f20315b199c17f21dc0a49ccd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"17\" /> ways to create subsets (consider including or excluding each number) and there are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420813c47b9ba0edd71bba84716bd485967ac81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> subsets only containing composite numbers (the composite numbers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/c/64c8cbc02382a70d36b3afcca0acbe8abeeb77c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4, 6, 8, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"60\" height=\"16\" />). Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/e/25eef6110375ebee24c7be3b4f870eaae006268a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^8-2^4=\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"156\" height=\"30\" /> total ways to have at least one prime in a subset.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Using_Answer_Choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Using_Answer_Choices)\">Solution 2 (Using Answer Choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Using Answer Choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Well, there are 4 composite numbers, and you can list them in a 1 number format, a 2 number, 3 number, and a 4 number format. Now, we can use combinations.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/b/fcbd6097655e8dd6c62dfc3ccdd910e5d632252c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{4}{1} + \\binom{4}{2} + \\binom{4}{3} + \\binom{4}{4} = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"257\" height=\"53\" />. Using the answer choices, the only multiple of 15 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ffa2b9b315ee5a817cb9adeef77289ca65aeef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>By: K6511\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Subsets of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f8440824a9efceca3bac830578ab38c27957f2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"18\" /> include a single digit up to all eight numbers. Therefore, we must add the combinations of all possible subsets and subtract from each of the subsets formed by the composite numbers.\n</p><p>Hence:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/1/f91460e471a08136687b7c236300cc78915df647.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\binom{8}{1} - \\binom{4}{1} + \\binom{8}{2} - \\binom{4}{2} + \\binom{8}{3} - \\binom{4}{3} + \\binom{8}{4} - 1 + \\binom{8}{5} + \\binom{8}{6} + \\binom{8}{7} + 1 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"734\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>By: pradyrajasai\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Total subsets is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f634b0cbc87a31125e5190eed0e1753e50e15128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^8) = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" /> \nUsing complementary counting and finding the sets with composite numbers:\nonly 4,6,8 and 9 are composite. Each one can be either in the set or out:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/0/420813c47b9ba0edd71bba84716bd485967ac81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4$\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" /> = 16\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/3/a33af0911c08e17695d2b368358dc797c53e7c1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$256-16=240$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ffa2b9b315ee5a817cb9adeef77289ca65aeef7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"75\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>-goldenn\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We multiply the number of possibilities of the set having prime numbers and the set having composites.\n</p><p>The possibilities of primes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a0543a630e07a452c6943582d286413668115f4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4-1=15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> (As there is one solution not containing any primes)\n</p><p>The possibilities of the set containing composites are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/8/9584bdb500d49089d884caad5e9f4484b6267bbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^4=16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> (There can be a set with no composites)\n</p><p>Multiplying this we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/80263f542e751eb0cd5cde342399ebe1b37e8bd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 \\cdot 16 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }240}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"148\" height=\"28\" />. \n</p><p>-middletonkids\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(HOW_TO_THINK_CRITICALLY!!!)\">Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (HOW TO THINK CRITICALLY!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/RkQPY-_Qieo\">https://youtu.be/RkQPY-_Qieo</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_1\">Video Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/6Bt4I23JL1s\">https://youtu.be/6Bt4I23JL1s</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=1609\">https://youtu.be/5UojVH4Cqqs?t=1609</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2018_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\